hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"18244","Affan narrated to us, Aban narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us from Zayd from Abu Sallam from a freedman of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Bakh bakh for five, how heavy they are in the Balance: There is no god but Allah, and Allah is Greatest, and glory be to Allah, and praise be to Allah, and a righteous child who dies and his parent seeks reward for him. And he said: Bakh bakh for five, whoever meets Allah Almighty certain of them will enter Paradise: believing in Allah and the Last Day and Paradise and Hell and resurrection after death and reckoning."
